Subject: Android STATIC_LINKING: take libdl/libm/libz from the NDK static archives

Why: the STATIC_LINKING=ON branch for ANDROID in src/CMakeLists.txt switches the linker back to
-Wl,-Bdynamic before -ldl -lm -lz, so the result needs the system libdl.so/libm.so/libz.so (the setup
of facebookexperimental/ExtendedAndroidTools, named in src/ast/CMakeLists.txt). android-linux-tools links
every tool that does not resolve host names fully static (ndk/REFERENCES.md, "Static vs dynamic
linkage"); bpftrace calls neither dlopen() nor getaddrinfo(). Without -Bdynamic the -static link takes
libdl.a, libm.a and libz.a from the NDK r30 sysroot.
Source: bpftrace v0.27.1 src/CMakeLists.txt (the two lines changed here); the non-Android branch below
it is unchanged.

--- a/src/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/src/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -202,7 +202,7 @@
 if (STATIC_LINKING)
   if(ANDROID)
-    target_link_libraries(libbpftrace "-Wl,-Bdynamic" "-ldl" "-lm" "-lz")
-    target_link_libraries(runtime "-Wl,-Bdynamic" "-ldl" "-lm" "-lz")
+    target_link_libraries(libbpftrace "-ldl" "-lm" "-lz")
+    target_link_libraries(runtime "-ldl" "-lm" "-lz")
   else()
     target_link_libraries(libbpftrace "-Wl,-Bdynamic" "-lrt" "-lpthread" "-ldl" "-lm")
     target_link_libraries(libbpftrace "-Wl,-Bstatic" "-lz")
